    "narrative": "Facing Misiorowski today, the Austin Waves offense faces a significant hurdle, as the opposing starter\u2019s 2.35 xERA dictates a high-difficulty environment that suppresses our overall efficiency scores. **Kyle Tucker** remains our primary offensive anchor despite a marginal score of 47.89. While his base projection is strong, the combination of facing an elite arm and a suboptimal eighth-spot in the lineup drags his output toward the bottom of our startable threshold. **Andy Pages** earns the final UTIL spot with a score of 43.07; while he lacks the platoon advantage we typically crave, his plate discipline and role in the lower third of the order provide just enough floor to justify the start over our remaining bench depth.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision was relegating **Luis Lara** to the bench. Despite a score of 33.85, he was the closest consideration for the lineup, ultimately failing to clear our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" due to a brutal matchup against Skubal, whose 2.85 xERA makes him one of the most formidable left-handers in the league. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** unavailable due to off-days or injury\u2014the latter remaining a major concern on the IL\u2014our versatility is constrained. We are opting to sacrifice potential volume from players like **Luis Lara** to protect our remaining game caps, focusing our assets on the few matchups where we aren't running directly into an ace-caliber performance. We continue to monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Liam Hicks** for any late-breaking lineup shifts that might allow us to optimize our categorical contributions, specifically in the stolen base department where our roster flexibility remains thin.",
